```cpp1
void countWordOccurrences(unordered_map<string, int>& wordCountMap, const string& textLine) {
    // Split the line into individual words
    istringstream wordStream(textLine);
    string word;

    while (wordStream >> word) {
        // If the word is in the word count map, increment its count
        if (wordCountMap.find(word) != wordCountMap.end()) {
            wordCountMap[word]++;  // Increment count by 1
        }
        else {
            wordCountMap[word] = 1;  // Add the word to the map with count 1
        }
    }
}
```
This function splits each line into words, then checks if the word is present in the `wordCountMap`. If it is, the count for that word is incremented by 1. If not, the word is added to the map with a count of 1.

